-- title:
--   A smooth integral Cartier section from local coordinates
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be uncountable algebraically closed of characteristic zero, $X$ integral compact and smooth of relative dimension 2 over $K$, $h$ = `sectionsMorphism k s hs` to a projective space, compatible with $X\to\operatorname{Spec}K$, such that locally $\Gamma(V)$ is a surjective image of a coordinate chart ring. For every nonzero polynomial $q$ there is $t$ with $q(t)\ne0$ such that the hyperplane section `projectiveHyperplane h t` has integral subscheme, smooth over $K$, and is locally generated by a regular element equal to the coefficient of $\sum_jk(t_j)s_j$ in a frame of $M$.
--
--   **Notation.** The iso-open of $s$ (`SectionOpens.isoOpen s`) is the union of the opens on which the morphism $s$ restricts to an isomorphism. `sectionsMorphism k s hs` is the morphism from $X$ to $\operatorname{Proj}$ of the graded polynomial ring in variables indexed by the sections, defined by sections whose iso-opens cover $X$, with $k$ the ring map from the base into $\Gamma(X,\top)$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The statement is verbatim from OpenAI's Lean development, with `Definitions` files of this development imported in place of the upstream modules; these are supporting code for the statement.
-- source:
--   OpenAI, Maximal Seshadri constants on arbitrary polarized surfaces, September 23, 2026, https://github.com/openai/math (paper: preprints/Maximal-Seshadri-Constants-on-Arbitrary-Polarized-Surfaces-September-23-2026/main.pdf; Lean: lean/OAI/AlgebraicGeometry/Seshadri, Apache License 2.0); Lean declaration `OAI.MaximalSeshadri.ProjectiveBertini.exists_smooth_integral_cartier_section_of_local_coordinates`, https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/AlgebraicGeometry/Seshadri/Projective/LocalBertiniSection.lean#L22

